  {
   "id": "thr_sweep",
   "type": "logic_python",
   "position": {
    "x": 3860,
    "y": 1460
   },
   "style": {},
   "data": {
    "label": "Python Node",
    "userLabel": "Threshold Sweep (F1/IoU/Youden)",
    "params": {
     "code": "// Threshold sweep — find the P(water) cutoff that maximizes a chosen metric.\n//   a = P (acc_mean image, 0-255)   b = truth mask (aligned GT)\n//   c = domain mask (opt)   d = metric selector (0=F1 1=IoU 2=Youden's J 3=MCC)\n//   e = threshold step (opt, 0.02)   f = bootstrap replicates (opt, 0 = off)\n//   g = semantic anchor threshold (opt, 0.5 = MC majority vote)\n// Replaces an eyeballed cutoff with the value that actually maximizes the\n// precision/recall trade-off against the ground truth. The optional bootstrap\n// band says whether the \"best\" threshold is distinguishable from the rest of\n// the curve, or the plateau is flat within noise.\nconst px = a.rows * a.cols;\nconst Pd = a.data, Pc = a.channels();\nconst Td = b.data, Tc = b.channels();\nconst Dd = typeof c !== 'undefined' && c ? c.data : null, Dc = Dd ? c.channels() : 1;\n\nlet metricSel = typeof d !== 'undefined' && Number.isFinite(Number(d)) ? Math.round(Number(d)) : 0;\nif (metricSel < 0 || metricSel > 3) metricSel = 0;\nlet step = typeof e !== 'undefined' && Number.isFinite(Number(e)) ? Number(e) : 0.02;\nstep = Math.min(Math.max(step, 0.002), 0.5);\nlet anchor = typeof g !== 'undefined' && Number.isFinite(Number(g)) ? Number(g) : 0.5;\nanchor = Math.min(Math.max(anchor, 0), 1);\nconst nBoot = typeof f !== 'undefined' && Number.isFinite(Number(f)) ? Math.round(Number(f)) : 0;\nconst metricNames = ['F1', 'IoU', \"Youden's J\", 'MCC'];\n\nconst Pv = [], Tv = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < px; i++) {\n  if (Dd && !(Dd[i * Dc] > 127)) continue;\n  Pv.push(Pd[i * Pc] / 255);\n  Tv.push(Td[i * Tc] > 127 ? 1 : 0);\n}\nconst n = Pv.length;\n\nconst thresholds = [];\nfor (let t = 0; t <= 1 + step / 2; t += step) if (t <= 1) thresholds.push(t);\n\nconst metricOf = (tp, fp, fn, tn, sel) => {\n  if (sel === 1) { const den = tp + fp + fn; return den > 0 ? tp / den : 0; }            // IoU\n  if (sel === 2) {                                                                       // Youden's J\n    const r = (tp + fn) > 0 ? tp / (tp + fn) : 0;\n    const spec = (tn + fp) > 0 ? tn / (tn + fp) : 0;\n    return r + spec - 1;\n  }\n  if (sel === 3) {                                                                       // Matthews\n    const den = Math.sqrt((tp + fp) * (tp + fn) * (tn + fp) * (tn + fn));\n    return den > 0 ? (tp * tn - fp * fn) / den : 0;\n  }\n  const p = (tp + fp) > 0 ? tp / (tp + fp) : 0;                                          // F1\n  const r = (tp + fn) > 0 ? tp / (tp + fn) : 0;\n  return (p + r) > 0 ? (2 * p * r) / (p + r) : 0;\n};\n\nconst prec = [], rec = [], f1 = [], iou = [], youden = [], mcc = [];\nfor (const t of thresholds) {\n  let tp = 0, fp = 0, fn = 0, tn = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    const pred = Pv[i] >= t, truth = Tv[i] === 1;\n    if (pred && truth) tp++; else if (pred && !truth) fp++; else if (!pred && truth) fn++; else tn++;\n  }\n  const p = (tp + fp) > 0 ? tp / (tp + fp) : 0;\n  const r = (tp + fn) > 0 ? tp / (tp + fn) : 0;\n  const spec = (tn + fp) > 0 ? tn / (tn + fp) : 0;\n  prec.push(p); rec.push(r);\n  f1.push((p + r) > 0 ? (2 * p * r) / (p + r) : 0);\n  iou.push((tp + fp + fn) > 0 ? tp / (tp + fp + fn) : 0);\n  youden.push(r + spec - 1);\n  // MCC uses all four confusion cells, true negatives included — balanced and\n  // robust to the class imbalance water always has.\n  const den = Math.sqrt((tp + fp) * (tp + fn) * (tn + fp) * (tn + fn));\n  mcc.push(den > 0 ? (tp * tn - fp * fn) / den : 0);\n}\n\nconst target = [f1, iou, youden, mcc][metricSel];\nlet rawBest = 0;\nfor (let i = 1; i < target.length; i++) if (target[i] > target[rawBest]) rawBest = i;\n\n// A near-flat curve makes the raw argmax an artefact: it lands on the first\n// point after the initial cliff. Taking the highest qualifying threshold is\n// just as arbitrary at the other end. The median of the candidates sits in\n// whatever plateau actually exists.\nconst TOL_FRAC = 0.99;\nlet candidates;\nif (target[rawBest] > 0) {\n  const cutoff = target[rawBest] * TOL_FRAC;\n  candidates = target.map((v, i) => (v >= cutoff ? i : -1)).filter((i) => i >= 0);\n} else {\n  candidates = [rawBest];\n}\nconst plateauFrac = candidates.length / Math.max(thresholds.length, 1);\n\n// When the metric is broadly flat, a run-to-run-stable, probabilistically\n// meaningful cutoff (the majority vote at 0.5) beats a ground-truth-fitted\n// argmax — provided snapping to it costs little. The cost is always reported.\nconst ANCHOR_COST_MAX = 0.03;\nlet anchorIndex = 0;\nfor (let i = 1; i < thresholds.length; i++) {\n  if (Math.abs(thresholds[i] - anchor) < Math.abs(thresholds[anchorIndex] - anchor)) anchorIndex = i;\n}\nconst anchorCost = target[rawBest] - target[anchorIndex];\nlet anchorUsed = false;\nlet best;\nif (plateauFrac > 0.3 && anchorCost <= ANCHOR_COST_MAX) { best = anchorIndex; anchorUsed = true; }\nelse if (candidates.length) {\n  const mid = candidates.length / 2;\n  const median = candidates.length % 2 ? candidates[(candidates.length - 1) / 2]\n                                       : (candidates[mid - 1] + candidates[mid]) / 2;\n  best = Math.round(median);\n} else best = rawBest;\nconst tOpt = thresholds[best];\n\nconst r4 = (v) => Number.isFinite(v) ? Math.round(v * 1e4) / 1e4 : null;\n\n// --- optional bootstrap 95% CI band on the selected metric ---\n// Resampling the domain pixels with replacement puts an uncertainty band around\n// the curve. If the best threshold's interval covers most of the curve, the\n// \"optimal\" cutoff is not statistically distinguishable.\nlet ciLow = null, ciHigh = null;\nout_ci = null;\nif (nBoot > 0 && n >= 30) {\n  const BOOT_MAX = 40000;\n  let sampleP = Pv, sampleT = Tv, m = n;\n  if (n > BOOT_MAX) {\n    // Deterministic subsample: a cap for speed, the interval width is set by\n    // the class sizes rather than by this.\n    let seed = 1;\n    const pick = () => { seed = (seed * 1103515245 + 12345) & 0x7fffffff; return seed / 0x7fffffff; };\n    const chosen = new Set();\n    while (chosen.size < BOOT_MAX) chosen.add(Math.floor(pick() * n));\n    sampleP = []; sampleT = [];\n    for (const i of chosen) { sampleP.push(Pv[i]); sampleT.push(Tv[i]); }\n    m = BOOT_MAX;\n  }\n  let seed = 12345;\n  const next = () => { seed = (seed * 1103515245 + 12345) & 0x7fffffff; return seed / 0x7fffffff; };\n  const draws = thresholds.map(() => []);\n  for (let bi = 0; bi < nBoot; bi++) {\n    const tp = new Float64Array(thresholds.length), fp = new Float64Array(thresholds.length);\n    const fn = new Float64Array(thresholds.length), tn = new Float64Array(thresholds.length);\n    for (let k = 0; k < m; k++) {\n      const s = Math.floor(next() * m);\n      const p = sampleP[s], t = sampleT[s] === 1;\n      for (let ti = 0; ti < thresholds.length; ti++) {\n        const pred = p >= thresholds[ti];\n        if (pred && t) tp[ti]++; else if (pred && !t) fp[ti]++; else if (!pred && t) fn[ti]++; else tn[ti]++;\n      }\n    }\n    for (let ti = 0; ti < thresholds.length; ti++) draws[ti].push(metricOf(tp[ti], fp[ti], fn[ti], tn[ti], metricSel));\n  }\n  const percentile = (arr, q) => {\n    const s = Float64Array.from(arr).sort();\n    const pos = (q / 100) * (s.length - 1), lo = Math.floor(pos), hi = Math.ceil(pos);\n    return lo === hi ? s[lo] : s[lo] + (s[hi] - s[lo]) * (pos - lo);\n  };\n  ciLow = draws.map((v) => percentile(v, 2.5));\n  ciHigh = draws.map((v) => percentile(v, 97.5));\n  const low = ciLow[best], high = ciHigh[best];\n  const within = target.filter((v) => v >= low && v <= high).length / target.length;\n  out_ci = {\n    metric: metricNames[metricSel], n_boot: nBoot,\n    ci95_at_topt: [r4(low), r4(high)], ci_width_at_topt: r4(high - low),\n    frac_thresholds_within_best_CI: Math.round(within * 1000) / 1000,\n    threshold_statistically_distinguishable: within < 0.5,\n  };\n}\n\n// The near-zero cliff is clipped out of the plot so the flat trade-off stays\n// readable instead of being crushed by the vertical transition.\nconst PLOT_MIN = 0.05;\nconst vis = thresholds.map((t, i) => (t >= PLOT_MIN ? i : -1)).filter((i) => i >= 0);\nconst take = (arr) => vis.map((i) => arr[i]);\nconst xs = take(thresholds);\nconst lowestMcc = Math.min(-0.05, Math.min(...mcc) - 0.05);\nconst pickTag = anchorUsed ? 'anchor ' + anchor : 'plateau median';\nconst fig = plot.figure({\n  width: 760, height: 480,\n  title: 'Threshold sweep — optimizing ' + metricNames[metricSel] + ' (' + pickTag + ')' + (plateauFrac > 0.3 ? '  [flat metric]' : ''),\n  xlabel: 'P(water) threshold  (t < ' + PLOT_MIN + ' clipped)', ylabel: 'Score',\n  ylim: [lowestMcc, 1.02],\n});\nfig.line(xs, take(prec), { color: [180, 119, 31], width: 1, label: 'Precision' });\nfig.line(xs, take(rec), { color: [14, 127, 255], width: 1, label: 'Recall' });\nfig.line(xs, take(f1), { color: [44, 160, 44], width: 2, label: 'F1' });\nfig.line(xs, take(iou), { color: [194, 119, 227], width: 1, dashed: true, label: 'IoU' });\nfig.line(xs, take(mcc), { color: [40, 39, 214], width: 1, dashed: true, label: 'MCC (uses TN too)' });\nif (ciLow) {\n  fig.line(xs, take(ciLow), { color: [150, 150, 150], width: 1, label: metricNames[metricSel] + ' 95% CI' });\n  fig.line(xs, take(ciHigh), { color: [150, 150, 150], width: 1 });\n}\nfig.vline(tOpt, { color: [30, 30, 30], width: 2,\n  label: 't = ' + r4(tOpt) + '  ' + metricNames[metricSel] + '=' + r4(target[best]) });\n\nout_curve = track(fig.render());\nout_optimal_threshold = tOpt;\nout_optimal_threshold_255 = Math.round(tOpt * 255);\nout_best = {\n  threshold: r4(tOpt), precision: r4(prec[best]), recall: r4(rec[best]),\n  f1: r4(f1[best]), iou: r4(iou[best]), mcc: r4(mcc[best]),\n  metric_used: metricNames[metricSel],\n  raw_argmax_threshold: r4(thresholds[rawBest]),\n  plateau_fraction: Math.round(plateauFrac * 1000) / 1000,\n  semantic_anchor: anchor, anchor_used: anchorUsed, anchor_cost: r4(anchorCost),\n};\nif (out_ci) out_best.bootstrap_ci = out_ci;\n",
     "color_index": 3,
     "node_note": "Balaie P(water) 0->1, trouve le seuil optimal (metrique choisie via d). a=P(acc_mean), b=GT aligne (out_gt), c=domaine(opt), d=metrique(0=F1 1=IoU 2=Youden), e=step."
    },
    "ports": [
     {
      "id": "image__a",
      "color": "image",
      "label": "a = P"
